POST http://localhost:8000/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Luis",
  "email": "luis@example.com",
  "password": "clave12345"
}

### Password numérico (espera 422)
POST http://localhost:8000/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Luis",
  "email": "luis@example.com",
  "password": 123
}

### Ruta inexistente (espera 404)
POST http://localhost:8000/otra-cosa
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Login correcto - espero 200
# Espero: status 200, body con data.id, data.name, data.email, data.role
#         NO debe aparecer password_hash
#         Header Set-Cookie: PHPSESSID=... presente
POST http://localhost:8000/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "luis@example.com",
  "password": "clave12345"
}

### Login con contraseña incorrecta - espero 401
# Espero: status 401, body {"error":"Invalid credentials."}
#         Sin Set-Cookie de sesión nueva
POST http://localhost:8000/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "luis@example.com",
  "password": "claveIncorrecta"
}

### Login con email inexistente - espero 401
# Espero: status 401, body {"error":"Invalid credentials."}  (mismo mensaje exacto que el anterior)
#         Importante: no debe revelar si el email existe o no
POST http://localhost:8000/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "noexiste@example.com",
  "password": "clave12345"
}

### Login sin password - espero 422
# Espero: status 422, body {"error":"Email and password are required."}
POST http://localhost:8000/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "luis@example.com"
}

